# Build context for the frontend image is this directory. Everything below is either
# dead weight in the context or a leak, and none of it is something the Dockerfile
# copies - this is here so that a future `COPY . .` cannot undo the care above.

# Secrets. .env holds the LiveKit credentials; a value that enters a build as an
# argument or a copied file is written into an image layer, where it stays readable
# forever. .env.example stays: it documents the variables and holds no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Installed again inside the image, from the lockfile, on the image's own platform. A
# host node_modules is the wrong one at best and shadows the right one at worst.
node_modules

# The build output. It is produced inside the image, and a stale local dist/ in the
# context is worse than no dist/ at all - it looks authoritative and is not.
dist
dist-ssr

# Version control and local environments
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.venv/
venv/

# Logs and editor leftovers
*.log
npm-debug.log*
*.sw?
.DS_Store
